  "articleBody": "It's easy to overlook safety in our own homes, especially in the bedroom, but sometimes a few changes can make a huge difference. Think about your walking paths: are they clear or do you find yourself constantly navigating around furniture or clutter? If you're tripping over rugs or have trouble getting in and out of bed, it might be time for an upgrade. Poor lighting, especially at night, is another big red flag. Can you easily reach your lamp or call for help if needed? Lastly, consider how easily you can get to essential items like a phone or water. If any of these sound familiar, a safety upgrade could really improve your peace of mind and prevent falls. You don't always need a major overhaul; sometimes, just clearing pathways, improving lighting, and making sure key items are within reach can transform your space. If you're unsure where to start or if the changes involve electrical work or structural modifications, it's a good idea to reach out to a professional who can help assess your specific needs and ensure everything is done safely and to code. It's about making your space work for you, not against you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
